  <title>4.18.1: Repeated Operations</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01188</md:content-id>
    <md:title>4.18.1: Repeated Operations</md:title>
    <md:uuid>c572d117-15de-4f96-a168-ffaf5ff89dbc</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><title>Warm Up Activity</title>
<para>Which one doesn’t belong?</para>
<para>A. \(5+2+2+2+2+2+2\)</para>
<para>B. \(5+6 \cdot 2\)</para>
<para>C. \(5 \cdot 2^6\)</para>
<para>D. \(5 \cdot 2 \cdot 2 \cdot 2 \cdot 2 \cdot 2 \cdot 2\)</para>

<!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
<exercise>
  <problem>
  </problem><solution>
    
    <para>Enter your answer here:</para>
  
  <para>Compare your answers:</para>

<para>
      Your answer may vary, but here are some samples.</para>
          
          <para>A doesn’t belong because:</para>
    
    <list>
      <item>
        It is the only expression with repeated addition.
      </item>
      <item>
        It is the only expression that only has addition.
      </item>
    </list>
    
    <para>B doesn’t belong because:</para>
    
    <list>
      <item>
        It is the only expression with both addition and multiplication.
      </item>
    </list>
    
    <para>C doesn’t belong because:</para>
    
    <list>
      <item>
        It is the only expression with an exponent.
      </item>
    </list>
    
    <para>D doesn’t belong because:</para>
    
    <list>
      <item>
        It is the only expression with repeated multiplication.
      </item>
      <item>
        It is the only expression that only has multiplication.
      </item>
    </list>
  
  </solution></exercise>
<!--Interaction End --></section>
</content>
